cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its derived feature tables in your research,
  please cite the manuscript (preprint / journal) when available and the
  software record below. Both are interlinked through the Zenodo deposit.
title: >-
  Battery Lifetime Prediction — SOP-Compliant Pipeline for Cross-Dataset
  Transfer with Conformal Uncertainty
authors:
  - family-names: Demir
    given-names: Durukan
  - family-names: Çoban
    given-names: Dicle
  - family-names: Sarp
    given-names: Salih
  - family-names: Çifçi
    given-names: Osman Safa
type: software
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline for early-cycle lithium-ion battery cycle-life
  prediction across four public datasets (MATR/Severson, HUST, Sandia/SNL,
  Luh/KIT) under a capacity-only feature contract. Implements within- and
  cross-dataset experiments with seven classical regressors plus a PyTorch
  1D-CNN baseline, MMD/Mahalanobis distribution-shift quantification,
  centered-log per-feature slope tests with BH-FDR correction, importance-
  weighted conformal prediction falsifier, SHAP×regime joint analysis,
  Kaplan-Meier survival audit, Hankel-DMD dynamics diagnostic, and
  MAPIE split conformal prediction with k-shot target calibration. Companion
  to a manuscript on cross-dataset transfer regimes and valid uncertainty
  intervals for battery RUL.
keywords:
  - lithium-ion battery
  - remaining useful life
  - cycle-life prediction
  - cross-dataset transfer
  - conformal prediction
  - covariate shift
  - concept shift
  - rank-signal regime taxonomy
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - reproducible research
  - Kaplan-Meier
  - MAPIE
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/osmansafacifci/Graduation-Project-Dicle"
